<<~ ahu slot=`#/placement-step-1`>>

! Placement step 1

Directory LOAD omits a source root `meta.mem` only when its parsed title names that source directory's bag declaration, which the catalog owns. Unrelated root `meta.mem` files, nested `meta.mem` files and other carriers still travel to the existing ingestion ward. Single-file LOAD retains its existing behavior.

The new wire-level regression first failed with `catalog declaration` in the dispatched carriers, then passed after the exclusion. A second regression first failed when an unrelated root `meta.mem` was omitted, then passed after narrowing the exclusion. At Step 1, `never-projected-never-ingests.test.ts` passed all eight checks, including the then-current forged receipt refusal. Step 4 retires that title-based ward under the operator's later placement ruling; the replacement asserts a receipt-shaped title lands as ordinary content only in the selected, granted bag.

Validation: recursive build and build stamp passed; CLI typecheck passed; `act-load-effect-split.test.ts` passed 11 tests; node `never-projected-never-ingests.test.ts` passed 8 tests; `tools/seed-census-witness.sh` passed (1154 files, 77 consumers, no open or stale); `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` passed. The full CLI suite before the final scope narrowing passed 1,823 of 1,824 tests; one `port-control.test.ts` grace-period test timed out under concurrent load. Its isolated rerun passed all 22 tests. The focused suite and typecheck passed after the final narrowing.

Relevant end-to-end candidates: `tests/e2e/load-tw5-filetypes.test.ts`, `tests/e2e/corpus-feed.test.ts`, and `tests/e2e/residency-create.test.ts`. These have not been run for this step.

Suggested commit subject: `lar:///placement.seed.excludes/root-manifest`

